 "_": "Jaw carrier — one part, section swept along X, 30 wide. Behind the block it is a tongue on the mid-plane (z ±4) carrying the Ø4 link pin; at the block it widens into a flange that backstops the block and is bolted to it (4 × M3 along Y, not drawn); the section then opens into a channel that wraps the rail, the block and the wall’s strip, with two feet either side that pass out through the wall’s slots; outside it closes into a web and ends in a 16 × 16 tenon standing 16 mm proud, with four M4 cross holes on an 8 × 10 rectangle — the finger mount. The pin hole is a cut along Z, the only boolean in this design. Built for the right side; the left is the same part turned 180° about Y.",
